WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.890
In the last days of June
2021, the village of Lytton,

2
00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:08.790
in British Columbia, reached
49.6 degrees Celsius.

3
00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:12.350
That set Canada's all-time
temperature record.

4
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:15.530
World Weather Attribution then
analysed the whole heatwave,

5
00:00:15.580 --> 00:00:19.930
across a region from
45 to 52 degrees north.

6
00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:22.910
Was it a normal, once-a-decade heatwave?

7
00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:25.870
Could heat like that have
happened without climate change?

8
00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:30.050
In this mission, you'll learn how
attribution science compares the odds of an

9
00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:34.570
event today with a modelled world
free of human-caused warming.

10
00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:36.870
Then you'll travel to the Horn of Africa,

11
00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:41.490
where five rainy seasons failed
in a row from October 2020.

12
00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:46.630
Your mission: decide whether Lytton's
49.6 degrees could have happened without

13
00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:47.800
climate change.
